        "mission_intent": "We need the systems security engineering team to develop a comprehensive continuous protection specification for the Meridian data-processing platform that ensures all data and information remain protected across every operational phase\u2014creation, storage, processing, and communication\u2014as well as during system initialization, execution, failure, interruption, and shutdown transitions. The specification must incorporate reference monitor principles so that every access request is validated, the enforcement mechanism is tamper-resistant, and we can demonstrate correctness and completeness through analysis and testing. Additionally, the spec needs to address secure failure and recovery behaviors, ensuring the system preserves a secure state during faults, errors, successful attacks, and during recovery into normal, degraded, or alternative operational modes. The platform also needs to support varying runtime configurations, and we need the team to use best efforts to guarantee that no time window exists where data is unprotected under any conceivable operational scenario, including scenarios we haven't yet characterized or threat-modeled. Please have the draft specification ready for architecture review by the end of next week, keeping in mind this needs to cover the full set of Meridian's twelve operational configuration profiles, three of which are still being defined by the infrastructure team and won't be finalized until next quarter.",
